implementationPlan.description:
RED: encode the repro as a regression row (test first). All runs use the approved prefix P = env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH="$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin". First record your own pre-change baseline: P node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs (at planning, HEAD 3aab4a62: 311 tests, 310 pass, 0 fail, 1 skip, ~42 s; siblings R13e/R13h/9eaa4c4e land rows in this file first, so use YOUR numbers), and the filed repro: P node --test --test-name-pattern='^CB3' scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs (expect fail 1: ReferenceError: Cannot access 'transferRefused' before initialization, plus an unhandledRejection from the orphaned framingCheck.run promise). Then, in scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs, add ONE row directly after the last row of the CQ-R13e1 bridge section (CB6 at planning). Name it with the next free CB number (CB7 unless a landed sibling took it; the name must never match ^CB3, so the child run cannot recurse). Exact prototype (verified red/green by the architect in a scratch copy):

// A row selected alone starts while this module is still evaluating, so it can reach only fixtures declared above it or hoisted.
test('CB7 CB3 selected alone fails only on behavior, never on fixture initialization order', () => {
  const env = { ...process.env };
  delete env.NODE_TEST_CONTEXT; // set inside a node --test file process, where it makes a nested run report to the parent instead
  const alone = spawnSync(process.execPath, ['--test-reporter=tap', '--test-name-pattern=^CB3\\b', fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)], { encoding: 'utf8', env, timeout: 60_000 });
  assert.deepEqual([alone.status, alone.stdout.match(/^# (?:pass|fail) \d+$/gm)], [0, ['# pass 1', '# fail 0']], alone.stdout + alone.stderr);
});

Error handling: every child failure mode fails this row loudly with diagnostics, never a silent pass. A hung child is killed at spawnSync's 60 s timeout (status null). A spawn error sets error with status null and empty stdout (match returns null). A TDZ or any CB3 failure gives status 1 and '# fail 1'. Each mismatches [0, ['# pass 1', '# fail 0']], and the assertion message carries the child's stdout+stderr. Reuse the already-imported spawnSync/fileURLToPath/assert/test (same idiom as the 'real CLI entrypoint returns JSON' row); no new imports, helpers or dependencies. Do NOT assert '# tests 1': Node 20 reports filtered rows as skipped tests (# tests 306). NODE_TEST_CONTEXT deletion is mandatory (inherited 'child-v8' makes the nested run emit v8-serialized reports, so the TAP regex never matches). Use the regex boundary ^CB3\\b (JS source), not a trailing space (no Windows argv-quoting question, never matches a future CB30). Run P node --test --test-name-pattern='^CB7' scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs and keep the RED evidence: fail 1, an AssertionError whose message carries the child's "Cannot access 'transferRefused' before initialization". If a landed sibling already made ^CB3 pass alone, name that commit, keep this row anyway, and take the red evidence from the scratch revert in the self-review step.
